  "optionExplanations": {
    "A": "Correct. Free air collects beneath the diaphragm and over the liver shadow on upright films.",
    "B": "Incorrect. A gastric bubble is expected in the left upper quadrant, not over the liver shadow.",
    "C": "Incorrect. Portal venous gas appears as branching lucencies within the liver, not a subdiaphragmatic crescent.",
    "D": "Incorrect. Gallstones are calcified densities, not lucent air under the diaphragm."
